WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.987
Interval scales support meaningful differences.

00:00:02.987 --> 00:00:06.172
Celsius temperature is the classic example.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:11.272
A difference of five degrees has the same interpretation anywhere on the scale.

00:00:11.272 --> 00:00:15.177
But zero Celsius is not the absence of temperature.

00:00:15.177 --> 00:00:22.082
Because the zero point is arbitrary, ratio statements such as twenty degrees being twice ten degrees are not

00:00:22.082 --> 00:00:23.837
meaningful.

00:00:23.837 --> 00:00:30.427
The easiest way to classify a variable is to ask what statements are meaningful in the real world.

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:35.812
Can values only be different, can they be ordered, are differences meaningful, and does zero mean absence?

00:00:35.812 --> 00:00:43.722
Those questions are more reliable than looking at whether the software stores the column as an integer or

00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:45.169
floating-point number.
